  "footnote": "Major courses require B or better; S/U is not accepted. Two-year Asian language proficiency requires testing into and completing the second semester of the second year, or testing into a course beyond the 2200-level. Placement and proficiency need departmental confirmation. Declaration: two Asia-content courses with B or better, at most one language course and no writing seminars; DUS approval required by the second semester of junior year (petition after the seventh semester begins). The college text gives an earlier sophomore-year declaration deadline; confirm with an advisor. Optional honors requires a 3.7 GPA in Asian Studies area courses, a senior essay and oral examination; apply in junior spring with a project outline and faculty endorsement. Senior fall research may use ASIAN 4401; an approved detailed outline precedes ASIAN 4402.",
